IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `miles-card-domain`
IMPORT `dbs-yuu`
IMPORT `dbs-womans-world`
IMPORT `citi-rewards`
IMPORT `hsbc-revolution`
IMPORT `uob-ladys-solitaire`
IMPORT `posb-passion`
IMPORT `flat-cards`

§ `Which card earns what — the composed answer`

-- ===========================================================================
-- THE COMPOSER. One exported rule, `the rate on`, dispatches on the card to
-- the issuer module that encodes that card's own document. It adds no rule
-- of its own: every figure, condition, citation and status in the answer is
-- the issuer module's, and this file exists so that a caller -- the consumer
-- app's generator, the MCP surface, the cheat-sheet assertions -- has one
-- signature to call.
--
-- WHY THE DISPATCH IS WRITTEN OUT PER CARD rather than routed through a
-- helper. The corpus must lower to Catala (spec section 2), and an exported
-- rule may call another exported rule directly but may not reach one
-- through a non-exported helper (CATALA-EXPORT-SPEC.md section 8.1.1). So
-- the CONSIDER lives inside the exported body.
--
-- DBS yuu is issued on two networks and its module reads `card` to tell them
-- apart (Appendix 1 treats the American Express card differently at named
-- merchants); both constructors route to the one module.
-- ===========================================================================

@export What a single card transaction earns on a named Singapore miles card, from the issuer's own terms: the rate, its conditions, the cap and its reset basis, the clauses relied on, and how far the answer can be trusted
GIVEN card       IS A Card
      cardholder IS A Cardholder
      month      IS A `Month position`
      txn        IS A Transaction
GIVETH A `Rate answer`
`the rate on` card cardholder month txn MEANS
    CONSIDER card
    WHEN `DBS yuu Visa`             THEN `DBS yuu earns on`              card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `DBS yuu American Express` THEN `DBS yuu earns on`              card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `DBS Woman's World`        THEN `DBS Woman's World earns on`    card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `UOB Lady's Solitaire`     THEN `UOB Lady's Solitaire earns on` card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `HSBC Revolution`          THEN `HSBC Revolution earns on`      card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `Citi Rewards`             THEN `Citi Rewards earns on`         card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `POSB PAssion Debit`       THEN `POSB PAssion earns on`         card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `UOB PRVI Miles`           THEN `UOB PRVI Miles earns on`       card cardholder month txn
    WHEN `Citi PremierMiles`        THEN `Citi PremierMiles earns on`    card cardholder month txn


§§ `Illustrations`

-- A household with Dining and Family elected on Solitaire, the yuu account
-- linked, no HSBC deposits tier, PAssion linked; a month in which the yuu
-- threshold has been met and the PAssion thresholds have not.
GIVETH A Cardholder
`the household` MEANS Cardholder WITH
    `Solitaire preferred rewards categories`               IS LIST Dining, Family
    `yuu account linked to the card`                       IS TRUE
    `HSBC Everyday Global Account deposits ADB this month` IS 0
    `PAssion membership registered and card linked in yuu` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Month position`
`mid-month, yuu unlocked` MEANS `Month position` WITH
    `yuu eligible spend so far this calendar month`                     IS 900
    `yuu participating merchants transacted so far this calendar month` IS 4
    `PAssion spend at Participating Stores so far this month`           IS 0
    `PAssion spend at non-Participating Stores so far this month`       IS 0

-- A tap at a Cold Storage checkout with the phone, on a Tuesday.
GIVETH A Transaction
`groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`           IS "Cold Storage"
    `merchant`                IS `Cold Storage`
    `merchant category code`  IS 5411
    `transaction description` IS "COLD STORAGE"
    `description patterns`    IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`             IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                  IS 80
    `currency`                IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`        IS YMD 2026 9 22
    `posting date`            IS YMD 2026 9 23
    `payment channel`         IS `Tapped at a terminal`
    `credential`              IS `A mobile wallet token`
    `merchant indicator`      IS Unknown
    `made in Singapore`       IS TRUE

#EVAL (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `miles per dollar`
#EVAL (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `miles per dollar`
#EVAL (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `depends on the merchant indicator`
#EVAL (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `miles per dollar`

-- The same four answers as assertions, so the Catala projection of this module carries test scopes:
-- a bare #EVAL lowers to nothing a `clerk test` can run, and an emitted module with no tests proves nothing.
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 10.08
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS Woman's World` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `depends on the merchant indicator`
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `HSBC Revolution` `the household` `mid-month, yuu unlocked` `groceries at Cold Storage by phone tap`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 0.4
